# Disturbed Slumber: "reach", checked from the other side. Bot2's Ornithopter (a flier) attacks on turn 2. Without the spell Bot1's
# Forest isn't a creature and can't block; Bot1 casts Disturbed Slumber (an instant) with Mox Emerald and Mox Jet in the declare
# attackers step, and the Forest, now a 4/4 Dinosaur with reach, blocks the Ornithopter and it dies. The "must be blocked" part asks
# nothing of Bot1's own blocks: the Forest isn't attacking.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Disturbed Slumber
Plains x3
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Disturbed Slumber.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Forest)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Block(Forest > Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Life = 20
